 The video also showcases our lightweight detection method based on noise entropy, which leverages differences in image noise residuals between real and synthetic images to enhance cross-domain generalization. Through concise animations and comparisons, the video emphasizes both the dataset’s scientific value and its role as a benchmark for advancing AI-generated image detection.\n\nLicensed to ACM for distribution via ACM DL and MM 2025 YouTube channel.\n\n[Input] iframe\n\n  * Download\n  * 469.82 MB\n\n## References\n\n[1]\n\nJinze Bai, Shuai Bai, Yunfei Chu, Zeyu Cui, Kai Dang, Xiaodong Deng, Yang Fan, Wenbin Ge, Yu Han, Fei Huang, Binyuan Hui, Luo Ji, Mei Li, Junyang Lin, Runji Lin, Dayiheng Liu, Gao Liu, Chengqiang Lu, Keming Lu, Jianxin Ma, Rui Men, Xingzhang Ren, Xuancheng Ren, Chuanqi Tan, Sinan Tan, Jianhong Tu, Peng Wang, Shijie Wang, Wei Wang, Shengguang Wu, Benfeng Xu, Jin Xu, An Yang, Hao Yang, Jian Yang, Shusheng Yang, Yang Yao, Bowen Yu, Hongyi Yuan, Zheng Yuan, Jianwei Zhang, Xingxuan Zhang, Yichang Zhang, Zhenru Zhang, Chang Zhou, Jingren Zhou, Xiaohuan Zhou, and Tianhang Zhu. 2023. Qwen Technical Report. arXiv:2309.16609\n\nCrossref\n\nGoogle Scholar\n\n[2]\n\nJordan J. Bird and Ahmad Lotfi. 2024. CIFAKE: Image Classification and Explainable Identification of AI-Generated Synthetic Images. IEEE Access, Vol. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAI-Generated Content (AIGC) for Various Data Modalities: A Survey | ACM Computing Surveys (https://doi.org/10.1145/3728633)\nciteturn36search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.4 years ago; Crawled: last week; ## ACM is now Open Access ... Published: 06 May 2025 Publication History ... AI-generated content (AIGC) methods aim at producing text, images, videos, 3D assets, and other media using AI algorithms. ... Despite the broad term of “AI” used in “AIGC”, the focus and progress of the AIGC field in recent years lies mainly on Machine Learning (ML) and Deep Learning 